            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exploring Some Geometric Themes"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here is a solid called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "octahedron",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", made by joining two square pyramids at their square bases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.391,
            0.139,
            0.63,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.391,
                0.139,
                0.63,
                0.319
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.357,
            0.634,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you visualise its net? This is one of its nets."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.391,
            0.384,
            0.63,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.391,
                0.384,
                0.63,
                0.528
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.535,
            0.787,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Taking all the triangles in the net to be equilateral, make a cutout of the net and fold it to form an octahedron."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.801,
            0.526,
            0.889,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.801,
                0.526,
                0.889,
                0.585
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.592,
            0.767,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As in the case of cubes, an octahedron too has 11 different nets."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.61,
            0.846,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So far, we have seen solids whose faces are all equilateral triangles (regular tetrahedrons), and all squares (cubes). Does there exist a solid whose faces are all pentagons? Interestingly, the answer is yes!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.665,
            0.847,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This solid is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "dodecahedron",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". This solid too can be made from a net! Mathematicians have been even able to determine exactly how many nets a dodecahedron has — 43,380."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.419,
            0.736,
            0.627,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
